{
  "layer": "solution",
  "type": "component",
  "name": "opencode-tool-plugin",
  "body": "The suite's opencode 2.x tool plugins: one plugin per tool file under `opencode-suite/tools/`, each default-exporting `Plugin.define({ id, setup(ctx) })` imported from `@opencode/plugin` and registering its one tool through a synchronous `ctx.tool.transform(editor => editor.add({ name, description, input, options, execute }))`. The definition carries the tool's name, description, a JSON-Schema `input` object, and an `execute(input, context)` returning `{ content }`; the `execute` closes over the plugin `setup(ctx)` context (and the tool's own optional `directory` argument) for the shared lib's load location. Each plugin's `id` is its tool's effective name (for example `apg_query`, `apg_rm`), unique across the suite. The suite holds one file per tool, so the install registry is file-shaped. Product source in `solution.container.opencode-suite`; `opencode-suite/package.json` depends on `@opencode/plugin`.\n\nimplemented-by: every `opencode-suite/tools/*.ts` plugin file and `opencode-suite/package.json`.",
